  "Question": "If the Highest Common Divisor of \\(6432\\) and \\(132\\) is diminished by \\(8,\\) it will equal:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-6\\)",
    "B": "\\(6\\)",
    "C": "\\(-2\\)",
    "D": "\\(3\\)",
    "E": "\\(4\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "The highest common divisor contains the prime factors shared by both numbers, using the smaller exponent for each shared prime. Here,\n\\[\n6432=2^5\\cdot3\\cdot67,\n\\qquad\n132=2^2\\cdot3\\cdot11.\n\\]\nThus their highest common divisor is \\(2^2\\cdot3=12\\). Diminishing it by \\(8\\) means subtracting \\(8\\), so the requested value is \\(12-8=4\\), choice E.",
